<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila official suggests new private pension fund.</title>
<headline>Manila official suggests new private pension fund.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Trade Secretary Cesar Bautista said on Monday he had recommended the creation of a private pension fund to help fund the country's $5 billion infrastructure requirement.</p>
<p>In a memorandum to President Fidel Ramos, Bautista said the fund can be patterned after Afores, a private pension plan scheme in Chile, to finance agriculture-linked infrastructure projects which private investors shunned because they they thought them unviable.</p>
<p>Agri-infrastructure includes farm-to-market roads and irrigation systems.</p>
<p>&quot;A new means of raising funds for this purpose is being identified with the assistance of Financial Executives Institute of the Philippines (FINEX),&quot; Bautista told Ramos.</p>
<p>FINEX is a group of leading bankers and financial managers in the Philippines.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
